@page "/components/drawer"

<PageTitle>Drawer — Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn</PageTitle>

<h1 class="doc-h1">Drawer</h1>
<p class="doc-lede">
    Structurally a <a href="/components/sheet">Sheet</a>. What vaul adds — and the only reason it
    exists — is that you can drag it shut, which on a phone is the gesture people try before they
    look for a close button. Past a third of the panel it closes; short of that it springs back.
</p>
<p class="doc-note">
    Snap points, non-modal mode and nesting were all written off here as things the platform
    could not do. Two of the three reasons were wrong. The top layer is a <em>stack</em>, so
    drawers nest; <code>show()</code> opens a dialog that is not modal. Only the drag itself
    needed building, and it is below.
</p>

